Keep associated fronthaul clients visible when STA SSID is absent.

After a successful BTM steer, the controller can report the station under its
new BSS with Associated=true while leaving the STA-level SSID empty.  The BSS
already supplies the authoritative SSID and haul classification.  Filtering on
the redundant STA SSID therefore hides a correctly associated client from both
/api/v1/clients and the topology overlay.

Classify the station from its parent BSS: require a non-empty BSS SSID and omit
all backhaul BSSs.  This preserves the intended fronthaul-only view before and
after roaming.

